1
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!

2
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

3
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:05,320
Joey, make a move already.

4
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,280
Okay, here you go, tough guy.

5
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,120
My rock ogre's gonna rock your block off.

6
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,270
Hmm.

7
00:01:14,353 --> 00:01:15,183
Yeah, I tell ya.

8
00:01:15,266 --> 00:01:18,709
Like that wimpy card has a
chance against my giant rock guy.

9
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:20,080
Give it up!

10
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:25,600
Guess I don't stand a chance unless maybe
I use the Breath of Light card. Huh?

11
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:27,980
Can she do that? Oh, yeah.

12
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:29,917
The Breath of Light
wears down, Rock Monster.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
It reduces them to rubble.

14
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:37,257
That brings your life
points down to zero, Joey.

15
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,117
Once again, you lose and I rock.

16
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,960
You stink at this game.

17
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:44,657
Tristan's right, Yugi.

18
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:45,720
I do stink.

19
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,489
I can't win a duel
monster to save my life.

20
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,700
What is it, Yugi?

21
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,115
Why can't I ever win?

22
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,065
Teach me what I'm doing wrong.

23
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:57,060
Well, let's start by checking
your deck, Joey. Huh? Okay.

24
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,440
Here you go. Yeah, thanks.

25
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:02,879
Powerhouse lineup, don't you think?

26
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,967
No one could win with these.

27
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,977
Joey, your deck's filled with
nothing but monster cards.

28
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:08,917
You got it.

29
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,717
I packed it with every
butt-kicking monster I could find.

30
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,800
But that's not how the game works.

31
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,797
Duel Monsters is all about
combining your monster

32
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,857
cards with your magic cards
to increase their strength.

33
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:24,058
With no magic in your deck, your
monsters will get creamed every time.

34
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,390
See?

35
00:02:25,473 --> 00:02:26,697
That's the kind of stuff I need to know.

36
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:28,839
Yugi, you gotta help me learn more.

37
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:33,297
My grandpa's the real
game expert in the family.

38
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:34,439
Maybe he can help.

39
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,911
Hey, Grandpa, I brought you a new student.

40
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:38,940
Huh? Student?

41
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:43,217
I was hoping since you know more
about Duel Monsters than anyone,

42
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,240
maybe you'd teach me. Teach you?

43
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,740
Duel Monsters is a very complex game.

44
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,257
Yeah, tell me about it.

45
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,157
Teya beat me three games in a row.

46
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,917
Actually, Teya beat you
five times in a row, Joey.

47
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,840
Five? Oh, man. Huh? Hmm.

48
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:00,574
Yes, I could teach you to be
a great tournament duelist.

49
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:03,397
But only if you're willing
to spend endless days

50
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:06,480
and sleepless nights filled
with rigorous training.

51
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,300
Ah, piece of cake.

52
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,560
With an attitude like that, teaching
you may not be worth my effort.

53
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,260
Nice going there, smart mouth.

54
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:17,897
Please, Yugi, help me convince him.

55
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:19,627
I will work hard, I promise.

56
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,357
Listen, Joey, teaching you duel
monsters is too big a challenge.

57
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,737
Even for my grandpa.

58
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,560
It's not impossible. Huh?

59
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,220
You mean it, Gramps.

60
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:32,757
Joey, he already said he can't do it,
and if he can't do it, he can't do it.

61
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,740
I never said I couldn't do it.

62
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,157
But if I agree, you must work hard.

63
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,920
I'll do anything. I promise.

64
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:39,870
I promise.

65
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,070
Fine.

66
00:03:41,153 --> 00:03:42,697
Then we'll begin your
instruction immediately,

67
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:46,662
my young friend, and believe me,
under my tutelage you will learn.

68
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,822
Now, can you name the most
powerful duel monster?

69
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,170
Uh, no.

70
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,497
Can you name the weakest?

71
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,410
No.

72
00:03:53,493 --> 00:03:55,469
You do know what a trap
card is, don't you?

73
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,510
Kinda.

74
00:03:56,593 --> 00:03:57,423
I have no idea.

75
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:00,897
Good evening, Duel fans and
our 10 million viewers at home,

76
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:03,357
and welcome to the Duel
Monsters Duel Dome,

77
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:07,558
where tonight the Duel Monsters
Regional Championship will be decided.

78
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:11,337
Of the 200 duelists that have
competed in this marathon tournament,

79
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,620
only two competitors remain standing.

80
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:18,740
Put your cards together for
Weevil Underwood, the Bug Brawler.

81
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,957
and his opponent the number one ranked rex

82
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:28,137
raptor dino duelist
bug boy versus dinosaur

83
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:31,837
breath what kind of match is that that
should have been me in there i know you've

84
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:35,477
been training for weeks but those guys are
in another league you're just not ready

85
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,257
yet sure rub it in and
on top of that you're

86
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,197
so tired you can't keep your eyes open i

87
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,797
think grandpa's lessons have been a bit

88
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:48,997
too tough for him so tired must rest you

89
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,397
have no time for rest did you come here to

90
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:54,457
learn dual monsters or
did you come here to

91
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:59,257
catch up on your sleeping
you see it's true

92
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:03,377
what they say you snooze you lose I must

93
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,897
have been nuts to think I could ever learn

94
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:09,300
this crazy game time for your
lesson What? We're not done?

95
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,620
Not by a long shot, you slacker.

96
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,160
Now quit your whining, Joseph.

97
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,497
I know you've been working long and hard,

98
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:20,197
but you really are coming
along as a dualist.

99
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,900
And I'm quite proud of you.

100
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:23,240
Gramps, thank you.

101
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:24,575
Oh, by the way, Yugi.

102
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:30,120
This package came for you. A package?
What is it, Gramps? I don't know.

103
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,791
It just came in the mail.

104
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:33,710
Huh.

105
00:05:33,793 --> 00:05:34,924
It's from Industrial Illusions.

106
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,757
Industrial Illusions?

107
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,937
That's the company that
makes the Duel Monsters game.

108
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:41,437
Why the heck would they be
sending a package to you, Yugi?

109
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,740
I have no idea.

110
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,957
Is it possible they heard
I beat the world champion?

111
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,720
You mean Kaiba? Yeah.

112
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,097
It wasn't an official match or anything,

113
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:53,415
but Kaiba did drop out of
the tournament because of me.

114
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:58,240
Draw your last pathetic card
so I can end this, Yugi.

115
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:02,037
My grandpa's deck has no
pathetic cards, Kaiba.

116
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:07,500
But it does contain
the unstoppable Exodia.

117
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:09,500
Ah, impossible!

118
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,400
Exodia, obliterate!

119
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,960
Just hearing Kaiba's
name gives me a headache.

120
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:27,240
Whoa, guys, Raptor just stopped Weevil.

121
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,149
Yugi, these guys any good?

122
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:32,037
Oh, yeah, they're both
pretty tough customers.

123
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:35,826
Weevil specializes in insect
cards and he's a great strategist.

124
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,617
Then you've got Rex Raptor
and his dinosaur cards.

125
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:41,760
He uses their power to
overwhelm his opponents.

126
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:47,820
Itsy-bitsy bugs against doing dinosaurs,
Raptor has got this one in the bag.

127
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,520
I wouldn't be so sure.

128
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,580
All right, Weevil.

129
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:55,880
Consider yourself dinosaur child.

130
00:06:57,400 --> 00:07:00,397
Oh, as Raptor plays the
strongest card in his deck,

131
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:02,560
The terrible two-headed King Rex.

132
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:06,232
Looks like this match could
be over right here, right now.

133
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,560
We're back, monster fans.

134
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:18,937
And with the two-headed King Rex in play,
it looks like this duel is all done.

135
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:19,860
Your move.

136
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,640
And all I have is this weak little buck.

137
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:29,397
Weevil Underwood counters
with a basic insect card.

138
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,720
He plays a wimpy bug
against a giant dinosaur?

139
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,977
The place will be covered in bug guts.

140
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:37,700
Maybe, but I wouldn't
underestimate Weevil.

141
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:41,340
King Rex, let's take this
championship. Stop him!

142
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,395
You've attacked your way into my trap!

143
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:50,597
But then, how could your tiny dinosaur
brain know when an enemy attacks,

144
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,856
my vortex activates?

145
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,160
Oh, no!

146
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,439
It's a trap guard!

147
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:58,220
Which totally traps your King
Rex in its inescapable embrace.

148
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,430
No!

149
00:08:02,513 --> 00:08:03,460
My King Rex!

150
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,117
And while he's trapped there,

151
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:09,180
I'll upgrade my basic insect by
giving him armor with laser cannon!

152
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,940
Not such a weak loot bug after all!

153
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:18,170
Attack!

154
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
And King Rex is extinct!

155
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,750
Wow!

156
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:29,663
Beat by a bug!

157
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:33,800
A stunning upset by Weevil
Underwood, our newest champion!

158
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:42,380
Man, King Rex squashed by an insect!

159
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:45,621
And now a very special
honor for our new champion,

160
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,677
here to present the Duel
Monsters Championship Trophy,

161
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:52,737
the creator of Duel Monsters and the
president of Industrial Illusions,

162
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:56,500
Ladies and gentlemen and
fellow duelists, I give you Mr.

163
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:59,200
Maximillian Pegasus!

164
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,081
Congratulations.

165
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,340
Thank you!

166
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,297
And as regional champion,

167
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:22,440
I invite you to compete in a bold new
tournament I'm hosting at Duelist Kingdom!

168
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,530
Mr.

169
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:34,477
Pegasus, with the announcement
that you made tonight,

170
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,997
we'll have thousands of Duelists
flocking to Duelist Kingdom.

171
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,910
Yes,

172
00:09:37,993 --> 00:09:39,657
and events such as this
will hopefully attract

173
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:42,640
those who possess the
Millennium Items I seek.

174
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,880
Which reminds me.

175
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,767
The package was delivered to the
boy just as you ordered, sir.

176
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,710
Excellent.

177
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,190
Ah,

178
00:09:51,273 --> 00:09:55,297
with all the excitement of the championships,
you forgot to open your package, Yugi.

179
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,420
What could it be?

180
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,230
Huh?

181
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,600
Some kind of glove. And stars.

182
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,371
Maybe there's an explanation on the video.

183
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,548
Pop it in and check it out.

184
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,030
Okay.

185
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,440
Greetings, little Yugi.

186
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:17,340
I am Maximilian Pegasus.

187
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:19,010
Pegasus?

188
00:10:19,093 --> 00:10:20,100
We just saw him on TV.

189
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:24,480
The famous Maximilian Pegasus
sends greetings to my Yugi.

190
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:28,700
I have heard some terribly
interesting things about you, Yugi.

191
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,090
Huh?

192
00:10:30,173 --> 00:10:33,320
Your impressive defeat of Seto
Kaiba intrigued me so much.

193
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:37,361
I've decided to investigate your
amazing dueling skills personally.

194
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,497
Right here, right now, we
shall hold a special duel.

195
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:44,698
We'll play with a strict time limit
of 15 minutes, and when time's up,

196
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,377
the player with the highest
life points will be the winner.

197
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:49,200
Are you ready here? What?

198
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:52,877
Well, he can't seriously expect you
to fight a duel against the videotape.

199
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:53,790
That's crazy

200
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,800
No, it's magic

201
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:03,177
Everything's growing dark and
cold and the others aren't moving.

202
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,257
What have you done to them?

203
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,752
Where have you taken us?

204
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:08,897
We're no longer in the world, you know,

205
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:13,000
but I will return you after
our game, but it's time to duel

206
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,720
Start the clock and
make your move, Pegasus.

207
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:35,080
Certainly. Let's begin.

208
00:11:36,020 --> 00:11:37,160
Nervous, Yugi boy?

209
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:38,240
You should be.

210
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:42,760
You have never faced a
duelist like me before.

211
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,041
You may be good.

212
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,637
I assure you, I am.

213
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:48,220
But I will beat you to save my friends.

214
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:51,500
You won't save anyone with
that dragon card. How?

215
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:55,079
I told you you've never
faced anyone like me before.

216
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,720
I know every move you'll make.

217
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,580
Before you can even make it.

218
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:09,997
Knowing every move you'll make gives me
a distinct advantage, wouldn't you say?

219
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:10,910
What?

220
00:12:10,993 --> 00:12:11,823
For example,

221
00:12:11,906 --> 00:12:16,171
I can anticipate your next play and
counter it with this dragon capture jar.

222
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:22,700
It will draw the Komori dragon from
your card and imprison the beast.

223
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:28,634
Trapped, never to be played against me.

224
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,000
This is crazy.

225
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:33,677
First he reads my mind, then he
brings the monster on my card to life.

226
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,817
This dark dimension we're in
is known as the Shadow Realm,

227
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:40,177
A mystical place where incredible
monsters can be summoned,

228
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,600
and the impossible is quite possible.

229
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,957
But what you're telling me can't be true.

230
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,517
Tell me, Yugi, do you believe
there is magic in these cards?

231
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,457
Don't you know?

232
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,677
You invented this game.

233
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,440
What if I told you I didn't?

234
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:56,940
In ancient times, the Egyptians
called this the Shadow Game.

235
00:12:57,560 --> 00:13:01,257
Powerful pharaohs would hold
mystical jewels in other dimensions,

236
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:03,737
just as we're doing
now, but not with cards.

237
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:07,660
They battled with real
monsters and real magic.

238
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:10,080
Magical forces so powerful,

239
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:15,040
the Egyptians lost control of them
and nearly destroyed the entire world.

240
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:19,008
It's a good story, Pegasus, but
these monsters can't be real.

241
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,406
Tell that to my Dragon Piper,

242
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:24,860
as his flute of resurrection
frees your Kumori dragon,

243
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,805
but puts him under my control.

244
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,080
I have to counterattack Silver Fang!

245
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,420
Oh, the heat!

246
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,490
Ha!

247
00:13:40,573 --> 00:13:43,940
As you see, Yugi, these
monsters are very real.

248
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,160
And also quite dangerous.

249
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:52,540
Ah, Yugi boy, you really
are quite entertaining.

250
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:54,880
The way you scowl and sneer.

251
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,667
So defiant and yet helpless.

252
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:01,640
And so completely ignorant of the
power of your Millennium Puzzle. What?

253
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:07,640
5,000 years ago, a powerful pharaoh
locked the magic of the Shadow Games away.

254
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,924
What's this have to do with me?

255
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:15,300
The pharaoh captured these vast magical
energies in seven mystical millennium items.

256
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:16,840
Seven items?

257
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:20,440
You're saying that my
puzzle's one of them?

258
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,717
Yes, and there are mystical
energies locked within it.

259
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:28,580
Magic that could change your life forever
if you only knew how to unleash it.

260
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:30,582
But why are you telling me this?

261
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:31,850
Why?

262
00:14:31,933 --> 00:14:36,417
Simply because I need you to know But
perhaps I have said too much And since the

263
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:41,600
clock is still ticking I propose we resume
playing Our little jewel He's right,

264
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,917
time's running out and I still
haven't figured out Whether

265
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,294
he can really read my mind
Or if it's some kind of trick

266
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,520
I've got to try something
Maybe my zombie warrior

267
00:14:58,380 --> 00:15:01,497
Wait a minute He definitely
knows what I'm about to do.

268
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:02,410
But how?

269
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:06,229
It's got to have something to
do with that weird eye of his.

270
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,356
That's it, isn't it?

271
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:14,497
That weird eye must somehow let
him see the cards in my hand.

272
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:18,177
So no matter which card I pick,
he's already one step ahead of me.

273
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:20,160
But that gives me an idea.

274
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,000
Hurry up now, Yugi boy.

275
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:26,160
Time is running out for
you and your friends.

276
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:30,249
Pegasus is expecting me to play
one of the cards in my hand.

277
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:33,381
But what if I play a card
even I haven't seen yet?

278
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:39,117
What happens if I draw a new card straight
from the deck without even looking at it?

279
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:42,620
I already know you plan to
play the zombie warrior.

280
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:46,257
And I'm already prepared
to counter it with a trap

281
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,620
card that makes even zombies
lie down and play dead.

282
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,380
Not this time.

283
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,277
I figured out your little game, Pegasus.

284
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,757
You may be able to see
the cards in my hand,

285
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:59,140
but you can't see the cards
I pull from the deck. Hmm?

286
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,420
My next card is...

287
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:03,240
The Dark Magician!

288
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:07,960
Ooh, the big scary Dark Magician.

289
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:12,700
Mock me all you like, Pegasus, but
my Magician will destroy that dragon.

290
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,720
Go right ahead if you think it'll help.

291
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:18,180
It'll do more than help, Pegasus.

292
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:22,673
It'll bring you closer to defeat and
bring me closer to saving my friends.

293
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:26,120
If it can do all that,
by all means, play it.

294
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,380
Dark Magician!

295
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,020
Dark Magic Attack!

296
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,480
Nicely played.

297
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:47,134
But by using your Dark Magician, you've
let me manipulate you once again.

298
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:50,580
By playing that one card,
you have ensured my victory.

299
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:52,170
No.

300
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,680
We shall see, Yugi.

301
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,720
Oh, a very rare card.

302
00:16:58,300 --> 00:17:01,040
This is the fearsome Faceless Mage.

303
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,560
I've never seen that card before.

304
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:07,697
But my Dark Magician is one of the
strongest magic cards in the game.

305
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:11,137
But how will he fare once
I combine my Faceless

306
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:13,920
Mage with the equally
rare Eye of Illusion?

307
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:17,020
Dark Magician, Dark Magic Attack!

308
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,000
Dark Magician!

309
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,100
My attack had no effect at all.

310
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:33,297
His faceless mage should
have been destroyed,

311
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:36,439
but it's still standing and
I'm running out of time.

312
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:44,538
I'm up by 300 life points, but only
because Pegasus is toying with me.

313
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:48,052
I've got to find a way to beat
him at his own shadow game.

314
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:59,637
Pegasus knows all kinds of
tricks But I gotta find a way

315
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:03,014
to defeat him I just have to
trust in my grandpa's cards

316
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,437
I attack your combo with the
Celtic Guardian This mighty

317
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:13,500
warrior will cut your faceless
mage down to size True,

318
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:16,237
your guardian is mighty
But you have once again

319
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:20,957
underestimated the incredible
power of my Eye of Illusion No!

320
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,460
Dark magic attack.

321
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:29,060
But that's impossible.

322
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,560
The faceless mage doesn't
have a dark magic attack.

323
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:33,600
Oh, no.

324
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:36,960
It was my own dark
magician that attacked me.

325
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:41,139
Pegasus is controlling him
with the Eye of Illusion.

326
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:46,667
But if he's using its magic to control
my magician, what's protecting his mage?

327
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:49,397
Well, Yugi, our time
together is nearly up.

328
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:53,960
And as I've more life points than
you, it appears I am the victor.

329
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:57,460
Time's not up just yet, Pegasus.

330
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:01,600
And you've left your faceless mage
vulnerable to a physical assault.

331
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:04,120
Summon Skull! Attack!

332
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:13,080
Hmm, well, we've run out of time.

333
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:14,457
But how close was that?

334
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:18,197
If you had been able to complete
that attack, I would have lost.

335
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,780
But I didn't, did I?

336
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:23,617
I have taken the measure of your
talents this day, Yugi Moto.

337
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:27,780
And when next we duel, we shall
play for far higher stakes.

338
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,100
I'm done with your games.

339
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:35,560
You presume I'm giving you a
choice in the matter, but I'm not.

340
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,697
For I, too, possess one of
the seven Millennium Items,

341
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,800
the all-powerful Millennium Eye.

342
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,380
A Millennium Eye?

343
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,037
That's right, Yugi boy.

344
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:47,840
And now I'll show you the
true extent of its magic.

345
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:53,460
You see, I have found that,
given the proper incentive,

346
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:56,200
anyone can be made to play my game.

347
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,230
Yugi!

348
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,150
Grandpa!

349
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:08,360
Yes, we will do again, Yugi.

350
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:11,855
How else will you ever reclaim
your grandfather's soul?

351
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:14,300
Grandpa! Grandpa! Grandpa!
